a local teen is graduating a year early  with honors from the top charter school  in the nation jeremy j ford spoke with  her and her family and shares her  incredible story tonight  i want people to see that through all  the adversities and challenges that they  can still make it on thursday keila  johnson will graduate with honors from  southeast career technical academy but  she says because of covid it wasn't an  easy task with the pandemic and me  graduating my junior year i didn't get  the chance to apply for any scholarship  her mother kiana johnson is proud of her  daughter and says her success is just  the beginning she dealt with a lot of  hardships she dealt with a lot of  challenges in her life like almost  losing her mother and co-parenting her  little brother when i first got to this  school freshman year my mom had a heart  attack that caused me to stay home from  school to watch my brother he's on the  spectrum he has autism but words of  encouragement enabled her to stay strong  and keep going she told me  just focus and she did graduating early  with a 3.6 gpa i want to see keala  continue with her success if you would  like to support kiela's journey to  college you can find the link to her  gofundme on our website at eight newsnow  dot com in las vegas jeremy j ford live  local now
 

